# GitHub workflow (dondron)

## Commit format

Use **Conventional Commits** with a DonDron scope:

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<optional body — why, not a file list>
```

- **Subject:** imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, ≤72 chars
- **Body:** 1–2 sentences when the why isn't obvious
- Pass via HEREDOC (see below)

### Types

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `env` | Docker, Dev Container, CI, dev tooling, dependencies |
| `feat` | New ROS nodes, packages, algorithms, launch behavior |
| `sim` | Gazebo worlds, SIL/HIL assets, simulation launch files |
| `bridge` | Micro-XRCE-DDS, PX4 ↔ ROS 2 integration |
| `model` | URDF/SDF, meshes, `dondron_description` |
| `docs` | `docs/`, README, run/build guides |
| `fix` | Bug fixes in any area |
| `chore` | `.cursor/rules`, `.gitignore`, repo scaffolding |

### Scopes

Pick the **smallest matching scope**. Package scopes mirror `ros2_ws/src/`:

| Scope | Paths / packages |
|-------|------------------|
| `docker` | `docker/`, `.devcontainer/` |
| `bringup` | `dondron_bringup` |
| `perception` | `dondron_perception` |
| `guidance` | `dondron_guidance` |
| `state-machine` | `dondron_state_machine` |
| `diagnostics` | `dondron_diagnostics` |
| `worlds` | `simulation/worlds/` |
| `repo` | README, rules, top-level layout (use with `chore` or `docs`) |

Omit scope only for repo-wide `chore` (e.g. `chore: normalize path casing in readme`).

### Examples

```
env(docker): add Jazzy Dev Container for macOS development

Enables node development on MacBook without native ROS install.
```

```
feat(perception): publish Detection2DArray on /detections
```

```
sim(worlds): add outdoor SIL world for Gazebo Harmonic
```

```
bridge: configure Micro-XRCE-DDS agent for Pixhawk UART
```

```
fix(guidance): clamp lateral setpoint when target leaves FOV
```

## Commits (process)

- Commit **only when the user asks** — never proactively.
- Before committing: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -3 --oneline` (match style).
- Never skip hooks, amend unpushed commits, or force-push `main` unless explicitly requested.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials).

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
env(docker): short subject here.

Optional body explaining why.
EOF
)"
```

## Push

- Push **only when the user asks**.
- Use `git push -u origin HEAD` for new branches; otherwise `git push`.

## Pull requests

- Use **`gh`** for all GitHub tasks (issues, PRs, checks).
- Before `gh pr create`: status, diff vs base, log, branch tracking.
- PR title: same `<type>(<scope>): <subject>` format as commits.
- Body via HEREDOC; return the PR URL to the user.

## Repo

- **Remote:** https://github.com/ruslan-ihnatenko/dondron
- **Default branch:** `main`
- Trackable work stays in nexus vault — not commit messages or inline TODOs.
